WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.348 --> 00:00:01.353
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

2
00:00:03.054 --> 00:00:04.222
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> Can I help you?

3
00:00:04.386 --> 00:00:07.645
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> Yes, I’d like a latte, please.

4
00:00:07.911 --> 00:00:09.510
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> Regular or large?

5
00:00:09.541 --> 00:00:11.068
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> Large, please.

6
00:00:11.293 --> 00:00:13.302
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> To have here or take away?

7
00:00:13.486 --> 00:00:14.644
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> To have here.

8
00:00:15.044 --> 00:00:17.452
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> That’s three pounds forty, please.

9
00:00:24.718 --> 00:00:25.660
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

10
00:00:27.802 --> 00:00:29.524
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> Where are my car keys?

11
00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.584
I can’t find them anywhere.

12
00:00:31.696 --> 00:00:34.186
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> I don’t know. In your jacket pocket?

13
00:00:34.381 --> 00:00:36.164
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> No, they aren’t there.

14
00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.019
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> How about on the hall table?

15
00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:39.198
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> No.

16
00:00:39.403 --> 00:00:41.145
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> Are you sure you don’t have them?

17
00:00:41.206 --> 00:00:42.682
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> Absolutely sure.

18
00:00:42.938 --> 00:00:44.342
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> Look in the living room.

19
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:48.964
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

20
00:00:51.136 --> 00:00:53.770
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> Oh no, it’s twenty minutes late.

21
00:00:54.446 --> 00:00:56.537
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> Is there a waiting room somewhere?

22
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:59.150
It’s really cold here on the platform.

23
00:00:59.406 --> 00:01:00.974
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> No, I don’t think so.

24
00:01:02.276 --> 00:01:03.751
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> What’s the time now?

25
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:09.070
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> Six fifteen. We can take the six twenty, but it’s a slow train.

26
00:01:09.387 --> 00:01:11.406
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> No, let’s wait, then.

27
00:01:14.265 --> 00:01:15.147
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

28
00:01:17.545 --> 00:01:20.711
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> OK, come on everyone, out here.

29
00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:25.067
Right, stand together under the tree. OK!

30
00:01:25.353 --> 00:01:29.309
Are you ready? Carole, I can’t see you.

31
00:01:29.412 --> 00:01:31.184
Can you stand next to Jim?

32
00:01:31.256 --> 00:01:32.793
OK, ready?

33
00:01:32.845 --> 00:01:35.068
Say cheese!

34
00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.012
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

35
00:01:42.313 --> 00:01:47.366
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> …So, Mr Bartlett. Do you have any questions you’d like to ask?

36
00:01:47.448 --> 00:01:53.074
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> Er, yes. On the website it says the hours are from ten to six.

37
00:01:53.453 --> 00:01:55.041
What about the weekends?

38
00:01:55.174 --> 00:01:58.638
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> The hours are ten to six at the weekends too,

39
00:01:58.782 --> 00:02:02.163
but you get paid overtime on Sundays.

40
00:02:02.286 --> 00:02:04.828
Saturday counts as a normal day.

41
00:02:05.115 --> 00:02:09.070
But if you work on a Saturday, you have a weekday free.

42
00:02:09.286 --> 00:02:15.393
The contract says clearly five days a week, with possibilities of overtime.

43
00:02:15.649 --> 00:02:16.654
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> Oh, right.